     - Regularly test the visibility and availability of the navigation elements in the UI to avoid discrepancies, especially after significant changes to the codebase. 

### Concluding Remarks:
When developing and testing user-facing applications, ensure that UI elements required for core functionality are consistently rendered and accessible. Avoid making assumptions about the presence of form fields or navigation links and actively validate these aspects during development. Implement vigilant session state management to ensure that user actions like editing notes and logging out proceed without issues. 

